WEBVTT

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:04.550
An inactive virus vaccine isn't feasible.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:07.480
And I'm not getting anywhere 
with a weakened variant.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.230
Damn it!

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.740
Give me one month.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.730
<i>Do I need to keep that promise?</i>

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.870
Experiments on living creatures 
are difficult, so...

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.090
Ow...

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.250
S-Sorry! I was thinking!

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.830
I'm fine, but...

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:33.260
A m-m-m-man!

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:36.760
What was that about?

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.200
My signature?

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.020
Yes.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.590
Here you go.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:46.520
Thank you.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.900
He's a pervert who attacks any woman he sees.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.060
B-Bye!

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.530
Pervert?

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.280
That's rather rude.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.950
You pinned a woman to the ground in 
the hallway back there, didn't you?

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:01.410
No! She...

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.910
Disgusting.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.920
You won't be getting all this attention 
just because you're a man for long.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.510
What does that mean?

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:15.300
<i>Mizuhara-sama, can we speak?</i>

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.680
Suou-san!

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.540
What do you mean you're not going 
to be my attendant anymore?

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:20.720
Mizuhara-sama...

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:22.220
You're...

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.040
Good, you're here.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.230
I'll introduce you.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.510
This is Katagiri Rea and Kuroda Maria.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.730
Your new attendants.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.330
What's going on here?

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:12.530
Mizuhara Reito, you are 
now famous worldwide,

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:15.610
and in a unique position compared 
to the rest of the Numbers.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:18.880
Thus, we're giving you 
more than one attendant.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.090
There's no rule saying you can only have one.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.950
Kuroda Maria is a researcher.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.810
Our technology director 
trusts her quite a bit.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.320
She'll be useful in your research.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.600
N-Nice to meet you.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:37.410
Katagiri will relieve Suou 
and see to your needs.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.540
She was a Citizen Relations Officer.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:41.490
Citizen Relations Officer?

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:46.700
Her job was to interact with the people 
on behalf of UW, and keep them pacified.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.840
She knows the outside world well.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.340
If you want to know something, ask her.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:55.080
I'll be going, then.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.090
Suou-san!

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.970
Why did you make her leave?

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.930
If you like her that much, 
just mate with her.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:09.890
I will not!

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:12.180
Don't get so mad!

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:17.330
As soon as the paperwork is finished, 
Suou Mira will no longer be your attendant.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:20.820
But she may still stay with 
you as a mating candidate.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:28.280
It's your fault she was forced to leave.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:34.640
Her most important mission was to get you 
to mate with as many girls as possible.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.840
She failed, so of course she lost the job.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.190
If you don't like it, then why 
not go mate with someone?

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:47.640
And while I'll permit you to 
continue your research into a cure,

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:53.350
if you're not going to mate with anyone, 
your other freedoms will be restricted.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.230
That's not fair!

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.220
Mira!

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.580
It's been a long time.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:03.610
Yes.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.590
You've lost weight.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.120
Take care of Mizuhara-sama.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:13.260
You don't need to worry about that man.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:16.870
He's just a loser who only 
thinks of women as tools.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.880
That's not who he is.

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:22.440
Goodbye.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.880
Wait! Listen, Mira!

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.860
If you let your guard down around a man...

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:31.220
You're as beautiful as ever, aren't you? 
Like time's stopped.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.400
Um, Kuroda-san?

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:40.000
Y-Y-Yes?

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.950
What is there where we're going?

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.860
It's called Keimon City. 
There is a hot spring.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.160
A hot spring? Is that all?

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.620
Um... somebody important in 
the MK Virus research field.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.120
Somebody important?

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.360
What are you doing?

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:58.620
Sorry!

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.610
I'll go change.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:08.260
You should just go over there.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:13.350
I'm not Mizuhara-san's attendant right now.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:17.780
You've got a difficult 
personality, too, don't you?

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.860
I'm sorry, Kuroda-san.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.360
No, I'm sorry.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:31.440
I'm not used to men.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:33.530
Is it okay if we try to 
be a little more casual?

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.120
We're close, age-wise.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:37.510
Okay...

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:41.550
Kuroda-san, you said you 
study virology, right?

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:42.630
Yes.

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:47.130
I know a decent amount about 
the MK Virus, I think.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.880
<i>The MK Virus was artificially created!</i>

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:54.160
How do you think it was born?

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:56.730
There are three theories 
on the origin of viruses.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:57.930
The regressive hypothesis,

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:01.890
The escape hypothesis, 
and the virus-first hypothesis.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.930
But we don't know yet.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:08.280
And since we don't know, "how it was born" 
may not even be the right phrase to use.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:14.400
It's possible that something that's existed for 
eons only just now came in contact with humanity.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:19.540
In fact, in biology, viruses aren't 
even treated as living creatures...

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.530
<i>She's suddenly much more talkative...</i>

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:25.290
Is it possible that a human made it?

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:28.910
You've got an interesting theory.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.060
Put on your clothes.

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:35.550
We might find some clues where we're going.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.850
Wh-What do you mean?

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:43.940
Keimon City is where the first victim 
of the MK Virus in Japan appeared.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.710
It's huge!

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:51.070
The lake's so big!

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:55.230
There's a group of students on a trip here.

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:56.580
But beyond that, we have 
the place to ourselves.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.920
I heard we're having 
spiny lobster for dinner!

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.970
Let's go play ping-pong! Ping-pong!

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:02.710
Forget that. Let's hit the hot springs!

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.290
We're not here to play!

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:07.540
This place is pretty...

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.550
I wish Mahiru-chan could've come.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.680
We can't let an outsider tag along.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:17.800
Creating an environment that relaxes 
Reito is part of your job, right?

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:21.360
My job is to manage his daily life

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.060
and help him focus on viral research.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.440
We disagree there, then.

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:28.190
Um...

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.980
That looks fun! Let me join in!

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.530
Knock it off!

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:42.610
I wish I could've gone into 
the open-air bath, too...

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.580
A holographic open-air bath!

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:50.840
This isn't bad either.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:57.860
Why...?

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:01.760
It's fine. It's more fun 
if we all go in together.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:04.980
There's no "Men's Bath" and 
"Women's Bath" these days.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:07.320
I'll leave...

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:08.230
Hold on.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.860
I'll wash your back as thanks 
for all the help you give me.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:15.090
No, you're the one who's 
helping me all the time!

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:16.620
It's the other way around!

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.370
Then maybe I'll ask you for help, then.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.780
Wash our backs.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:31.280
It's so nice, having Reito-sama wash my back!

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:33.950
Okay, all clean.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:35.510
Thank you!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.990
G-Go ahead.

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:41.790
O-Okay...

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.200
<i>She's like a different person.</i>

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:47.200
<i>Does her personality change when 
she's talking about the virus?</i>

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:51.900
Sorry! Was it too hot?

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.280
I'll do the rest myself.

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:57.320
Go ahead.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.280
Sit down.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:09.040
<i>She has such a pretty back.</i>

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.130
Why not have him wash yours, too?

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:12.510
Not a chance.

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.800
Okay, I'm last, then.

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:17.570
It's finally over...

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:19.090
Not that.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:23.600
My skin is sensitive. 
Will you wash me with your hands?

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:30.850
That feels so good. You're good at this.

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:33.110
I-I'll wash it off.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:36.360
Not yet. Here, too.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.370
You can do the legs, too, can't you?

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:46.870
Run your hands over every little bit.

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.480
And lastly this.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:54.480
I'm leaving!

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:56.630
Do the rest yourself!

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:59.190
And I was so close, too.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:05.640
It's been so long since 
I've seen Ms. Taniguchi.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:09.140
I'm Katagiri Rea with UW's Japan branch.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:09.890
This is...

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:11.180
I know.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:15.510
We're here to talk about your husband...

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:18.650
I told you everything I could.

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.270
I saw your press conference.

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:22.410
Thank you.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:25.210
But it's not my problem.

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:29.410
My husband's not coming back, 
even if you do make a cure.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:33.310
Taniguchi-san, can you 
tell us what your husband

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:37.340
was doing just before 
he contracted the virus?

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:38.050
No.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:40.800
Please! This is for all humanity's sake!

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.680
You took his body and sliced it into pieces!

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:48.210
Ma'am, that's called an autopsy. We have 
to do it to find out what happened...

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:49.720
I don't care.

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:52.560
He hated doctors.

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:54.230
Taniguchi-san!

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.560
Don't touch me.

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:58.320
What do I have to do to get you to help me?

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:02.040
You can screw me.

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:04.820
I'm joking, of course.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.260
Leave.

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:14.500
The MK Virus appeared in multiple 
spots all around the world at once.

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:17.410
There's a theory that it was bioterrorism 
by a nation-state or terrorist group.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:18.770
A theory it arose naturally.

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:22.760
And even a theory that the Earth 
itself created it to purge humanity.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.680
But we don't know where it came from.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:31.640
Ms. Taniguchi's husband was 
the first victim in Japan.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:37.020
<b>Episode 5</b>

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:37.020
<b>First Victim</b>

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:36.520
He hated technology and had no GPS on him.

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.890
If we knew what he was doing and where he was

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:43.290
before he got sick, 
it might give us a clue, but...

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:47.000
She greatly distrusts UW.

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:50.170
The government at the time was really rough.

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:57.290
The person you care about was here.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:01.820
Why not meet him, Erisa?

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.720
<b>Keimon City Central Hospital</b>

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:05.720
You never learn.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.690
It doesn't matter how many times 
you come. It won't change a thing.

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:08.720
Please!

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:13.850
If we know what your husband was doing, 
we might know where the virus came from!

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:17.980
You should just stop making 
vaccines and start making kids.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:22.730
Your biggest job right now is making kids.

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:26.360
I'm sure you're having some fun with 
the crowd of girls behind you, though.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:27.910
I'm...

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:34.750
Mizuhara hasn't mated, that is, had any 
sexual relations with women after waking up.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.880
The rest of you, leave.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.630
I don't get it.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:47.680
Most people in your situation would be going 
at it like a rabbit with any girl he could find.

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:51.140
You'd have enough time left 
over to research the medicine.

00:13:51.590 --> 00:13:53.490
I don't have the kind of 
personality you'd need

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:56.770
to be having fun with girls 
while doing research.

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.680
You gay?

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:00.210
No.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.250
There are a lot of girls who are very pretty.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:05.400
And honestly, I'd love to 
do what they want me to.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:06.870
So why?

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:09.240
That's what would benefit the world the most.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.530
There's a girl I'm in love with.

00:14:14.350 --> 00:14:16.990
I know it's selfish,

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:22.250
but I figured if I put my efforts into 
finding a cure for the MK Virus,

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:25.760
it would make up for it.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:30.300
We're done talking.

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:44.400
It feels so good to be outside!

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:49.530
If Rea-san finds out I brought you to the 
open-air bath, she'll get mad at me!

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:52.220
It's fine! Nobody's here.

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:55.160
Don't blame me if something happens.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:58.420
<i>Taniguchi-san managed to 
avoid telling me anything.</i>

00:14:58.420 --> 00:14:59.530
Come on, hurry!

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:01.170
Reito-sama, hide!

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:05.050
Um, this bath is in use...

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:06.240
She's so cute!

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:07.690
The students?

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:11.610
I'll just have to hide in here for a little.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:15.560
Oh!

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:18.220
U-Um...

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:23.820
I'll be going—

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:25.860
Leave, and I'll scream.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:30.490
If you don't want to 
cause a ruckus, sit down.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:33.240
Why are you wearing a yukata in the sauna?

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:37.270
Because I'm an exchange 
student that loves Japan!

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:40.060
The rich depths of the Japanese heart!

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:41.500
<i>I don't think that's how it works.</i>

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:44.750
Now, let's play a game.

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:51.630
If I leave the sauna first, 
I won't tell anybody you're here.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.390
And if I leave first...

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:59.890
You'll have to do one thing I tell 
you to do, Mizuhara Reito-san.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:02.770
<i>She knows me. Of course she would.</i>

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:05.680
Let's see who can last longer.

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:13.780
It's so hot.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:15.690
I should introduce myself.

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:20.290
I'm Chloe. I'm an exchange 
student from America.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:23.230
Y-Your Japanese is very good.

00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:25.290
A little weird, but good.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:28.800
I love Japan.

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:32.050
Would you like to have sex with me?

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:35.930
Oh, you call it "mating," right?

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:39.680
